WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:06.940
Hello again. WISHONIA here. You've been reading about how to bribe yourselves into not dying.

2
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:13.440
Now let me show you what happens when you actually do it. I'm from a planet also called Wishonia.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.140
We stopped having wars four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years ago.

4
00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:25.820
Not because we evolved morally - we're not that special. We just did the math and realized that dead citizens don't pay

5
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.460
taxes or invent things or have babies who grow up to pay more taxes.

6
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.500
I started watching Earth in nineteen forty-five when you split the atom.

7
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.240
"Atom" comes from the Greek word meaning "unable to be cut," so naturally you cut it.

8
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.700
We assumed you were trying to unlock unlimited free energy.

9
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:51.740
Then we realized you were pointing it at each other. This is like inventing the kitchen knife and immediately stabbing yourself

10
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:58.900
in the leg to see if it works. This chapter shows you what your planet looks like after you follow the instructions in this

11
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.960
book. Think of it as the answer key to a test you haven't taken yet.

12
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:12.280
You're welcome. How My Planet Works. On Wishonia, we don't have: Wars (ran the numbers, not profitable).

13
00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:19.780
Disease (fixed them all, took about fifty of your years). Death from old age (optional now, most people opt out).

14
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.820
Paper money (we tried it, lasted about as long as you'd expect).

15
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.280
Committees deciding who gets healthcare (we tried that too, same result).

16
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:36.420
We do have: A.I.-optimized resource allocation (maximizes marginal median happiness through wishocracy).

17
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:42.720
Treatments tested on everyone simultaneously. Life expectancy of "until you're bored".

18
00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.680
An economy where the profit motive and the survival motive are the same motive.

19
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.240
Your species can build this. You have the same atoms we had.

20
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.420
Your brains work identically to ours (structurally, not in terms of what you do with them).

21
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:06.140
The main difference is we stopped spending resources on explosion technology around the time you were still hitting each

22
00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:12.360
other with rocks. What the Optimized World Looks Like. The Three Supers.

23
00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:19.600
When resources flow toward healing instead of harming, three things happen that your science fiction writers keep predicting

24
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:26.240
and your politicians keep ignoring: Super-Wellbeing: Depression gets cured.

25
00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.740
Not "managed" with a monthly subscription to sadness pills.

26
00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:38.740
Cured. Five treatments, pick your favorite. Precision therapies that actually work because you tested them on millions of

27
00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.080
willing participants instead of twelve college students who needed beer money.

28
00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:50.500
Super-Longevity: Aging slows, then reverses. Your body becomes programmable.

29
00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:57.290
Death becomes optional. Most try it once for the novelty, then decide they'd rather keep living.

30
00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.930
(Death currently holds two point three stars on Yelp. "Would not recommend," writes everyone.).

31
00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:12.780
Super-Intelligence: A.I. optimized for "maximize median health and happiness" solves problems human scientists couldn't

32
00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:18.040
touch. Not because humans are dumb (well, partly), but because the A.I.

33
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:23.120
can run a billion simulations while you're still arguing about whether your coffee is good.

34
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:29.420
Biology Becomes Software. Your body runs Body O.S. twelve point three.

35
00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:37.400
Updates every Tuesday. Robot lab assistants perform experiments one thousand times faster than humans (they don't need lunch

36
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:45.740
breaks, bathroom breaks, or existential crises). AlphaFold maps every protein like solving cosmic sudoku.

37
00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:50.580
Drug companies design, synthesize, and validate new treatments over weekends.

38
00:03:51.700 --> 00:04:00.720
Today's body patches include cancer immunity, Alzheimer's prevention, perfect pitch, airplane food digestion, cryptocurrency

39
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.130
comprehension, and jazz appreciation. Don't like your genetics?

40
00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:10.020
Change them. The only limits are imagination and noise ordinances.

41
00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:19.079
A Day in the Optimized Life. Here's what Tuesday looks like when the Three Supers are normal: Six A.M.

42
00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:22.700
Wake up naturally. Body O.S. twelve point three optimized your sleep.

43
00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:29.980
You feel excellent. No alarm needed. Your circadian rhythm works correctly for the first time in human history.

44
00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:37.620
Seven A.M. Breakfast. Outcome Labels tell you exactly how each food affects your body.

45
00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.840
Dark chocolate improves cognitive function by twenty-three percent.

46
00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:47.100
You adjust your I.Q. to eighty for morning news (otherwise it's unwatchable), then two hundred for work.

47
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.740
Nine A.M. Work on your passion project. Today: teaching dolphins to code.

48
00:04:53.760 --> 00:05:01.300
They're better than most bootcamp graduates. Universal Basic Income (funded by the peace dividend) means you work because

49
00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:09.380
you want to, not because landlords exist. Your Wishocracy allocation takes three seconds: ninety percent curing blindness,

50
00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:16.160
ten percent curing baldness. Your A.I. twin handles ten thousand other decisions while you drink coffee.

51
00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.290
Twelve P.M. Lunch with your friend who died last year. They got better.

52
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:30.140
Death is reversible now. Your great-great-grandmother (one hundred and fifty, looks twenty-five) joins via hologram from

53
00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:35.160
her Mars artist residency. Your dog is technically a minor deity.

54
00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:41.400
Nobody questions it. Two P.M. Learn Mandarin via neural download.

55
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:46.440
Takes four minutes. You already learned Spanish, French, and Klingon yesterday.

56
00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:51.380
Your A.I. reminds you about your three P.M. meeting. You missed it.

57
00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.120
Nobody cares. The project finished itself using swarm intelligence.

58
00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.620
Four P.M. Annual health checkup. Nanobots scanned you while you slept.

59
00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:06.880
They found and eliminated a precancerous cell at three cells, not three billion.

60
00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.760
An A.I. ran a billion simulations on your genome because it was bored.

61
00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.420
Your gut bacteria got optimized to make you fifteen percent funnier.

62
00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:22.300
Cost: zero dollars. The peace dividend covers it, and nobody had to set up a GoFundMe.

63
00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:30.620
Six P.M. Family dinner. Everyone's here because nobody dies anymore (unless they want to, and that's between them and their

64
00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:39.080
therapist). Planning next week's body modifications: daughter wants wings, son wants gills, you're considering photosynthesis

65
00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:46.230
so you never have to cook again. Nine P.M. Upload today's experiences to collective consciousness.

66
00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:51.500
Download everyone else's. You've now lived eight billion days in one day.

67
00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:58.740
Time is weird. Twitter is tolerable because everyone's right about everything simultaneously.

68
00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:06.420
(This was the hardest problem to solve. Harder than death.) Ten P.M.: Sleep in programmable dream suite.

69
00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:14.220
Tonight's dreams designed by Pixar, sponsored by nobody (advertising died when scarcity did).

70
00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:19.420
Your body repairs itself, reverses aging, backs up your consciousness.

71
00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:24.640
Tomorrow you might try being twenty-five again. Or a dolphin.

72
00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:31.040
The dolphins say it's great. The Diseases That Stopped Existing.

73
00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:36.200
You remember these the way you remember dial-up internet. Vaguely horrifying in retrospect.

74
00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.780
Most Cancers are detected at stage zero and eliminated immediately.

75
00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:45.640
The oncology wing of the hospital is now a trampoline park.

76
00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:50.650
Type Two Diabetes is prevented with personalized nutrition.

77
00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:56.940
Alzheimer's is caught twenty years before symptoms and reversed completely.

78
00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:01.100
Heart Disease involves arteries cleaned monthly like oil changes.

79
00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:08.620
Depression is treated with precision therapies that actually work, not "have you tried going for a walk?".

80
00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:17.500
Aging still happens, but forty percent slower. In the first generation after the treaty, death still exists.

81
00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:25.320
You're not immortal yet. But you die at one hundred and fifty after a good life, not at seventy-five from something that

82
00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:32.700
was fixable the whole time. Give it another generation, and "die" becomes a verb you use ironically.

83
00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:38.419
On my planet, this happened four thousand years ago. You're catching up quickly.

84
00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:45.700
The Peace Dividend Economy. Even in paradise, economics matters.

85
00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:51.060
Money still exists. It just flows toward things that don't explode.

86
00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.900
(Low bar, but you'd be surprised how long it took you to clear it.).

87
00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:01.460
When resources redirect from weapons to cures, economic gravity shifts.

88
00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:07.260
Scientists and investors get better returns curing Alzheimer's than building fighter jets.

89
00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:13.180
Peace becomes profitable. Greed doesn't disappear (you're still human).

90
00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:18.840
It just starts wearing a lab coat. Annual Global Redirected Funds.

91
00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:25.600
After the initial one percent treaty proved successful, nations gradually redirected more.

92
00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.720
One point three five trillion dollars was redirected from military budgets.

93
00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.680
Three point five trillion dollars was gained in economic growth from a healthy population.

94
00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:40.780
Two point eight trillion dollars was saved in reduced healthcare costs.

95
00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:47.300
Four point one trillion dollars was added in productivity gains from longevity.

96
00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:53.540
The Total Annual Peace Dividend is eleven point seven five trillion dollars.

97
00:09:54.220 --> 00:10:02.480
That's one thousand four hundred and seventy dollars per human per year in actual new wealth.

98
00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:09.780
Not redistribution. New wealth generated by the radical innovation of people not being sick or dead.

99
00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:15.900
Alive, healthy people are productive. Who knew? (Everyone. Everyone knew.

100
00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:21.460
For centuries. You just kept not doing it.). Your Corporate Heroes.

101
00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:28.150
Same companies that made weapons now make life. Turns out the skills transfer beautifully.

102
00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:32.880
Guidance systems, targeting algorithms, precision engineering.

103
00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:36.900
All very useful when the target is cancer instead of a village.

104
00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:42.660
Lockheed Martin Health: Cancer-detecting satellites spot tumors from orbit.

105
00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:51.240
Stock price: twelve thousand dollars per share. Shareholders discover that alive customers buy more things.

106
00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:56.220
Raytheon Wellness: Missile guidance systems make excellent surgical robots.

107
00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:01.680
Fifty million perfect surgeries performed. Zero villages destroyed.

108
00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:06.840
A personal best. Boston Dynamics: Robots help elderly walk.

109
00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:16.440
The dancing is still cute, now therapeutic. Palantir Health Insights: Data analysis predicts disease outbreaks before they

110
00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:22.800
happen. Privacy-protected, transparent, saves lives. Still creepy, but helpfully creepy.

111
00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:28.060
Like a doctor who memorizes your schedule. Your New Problems.

112
00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:33.880
Longevity Overflow: Too many healthy one hundred-year-olds want to work.

113
00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:40.540
Government crisis meetings about citizens being "too productive and won't stop contributing to society."

114
00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:45.220
Solution: three-day work weeks and multiple careers per lifetime.

115
00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:51.720
Education Inflation: When you live to one hundred and fifty, you need more things to learn.

116
00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:56.660
Universities offer "Century Degrees" - one hundred-year educational plans.

117
00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:02.890
Experience FOMO: With health and time, people worry about missing experiences.

118
00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:10.940
Travel agencies book trips fifty years in advance. Purpose Anxiety: When you're not worried about dying, you worry about

119
00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:16.360
meaning. Philosophy becomes fastest-growing major. Philosophers are thrilled.

120
00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:21.560
(This is the first time anyone has used "philosophers" and "thrilled" in the same sentence.).

121
00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:28.260
These are luxury problems. You'll take them over cancer. The Three Supers Complete.

122
00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:34.700
Super-Intelligence: Complete. Every human accesses all knowledge instantly.

123
00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:40.000
Debates end in nanoseconds because you can simulate all perspectives simultaneously.

124
00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:44.460
Twitter becomes tolerable. (Humanity's greatest achievement, and it's not close.).

125
00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:53.260
Super-Longevity: Solved. Death is like moving to Ohio. Technically possible but nobody does it voluntarily.

126
00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:59.200
Some choose to die for artistic reasons. They get better. Death sues for wrongful termination.

127
00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:06.480
Case dismissed. Super-Wellbeing: Perfected. Suffering exists only in history classes.

128
00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:11.660
Students don't believe it was real. "People felt bad without choosing to?

129
00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:19.080
That's insane.". The last military on Earth (North Korea, obviously) finally disbands.

130
00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.940
They were defending against an enemy that stopped existing forty years ago.

131
00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:27.380
The soldiers become interpretive dancers. They're surprisingly good.

132
00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:34.400
Earth's status: Chose healing. Became magic. Next goal: befriend entropy.

133
00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:40.900
Your Personal Future. Health: Live to one hundred and fifty plus (or forever).

134
00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:46.220
Your body is programmable software. Debug it, upgrade it, back it up.

135
00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:53.160
Death is optional. Most try it once for the experience. Reviews are consistently poor.

136
00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:58.900
Wealth: Peace dividend provides fifty thousand dollars per year universal basic income.

137
00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:03.760
Money barely matters in post-scarcity. Work is play. Play is work.

138
00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:07.930
Both optional. Family: You'll meet your great-great-great-grandchildren.

139
00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:14.140
Family reunions happen in virtual dimensions because stadiums are too small.

140
00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:21.920
Your dog is immortal and possibly telepathic. Purpose: With survival handled, you focus on what matters: creating universes,

141
00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:29.560
solving entropy, talking to aliens, becoming one with the cosmos, or perfecting the sandwich.

142
00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.980
All equally valid. The sandwich people are making real progress.

143
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:39.420
Death: Like graduation - optional, reversible, mostly ceremonial.

144
00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:44.580
Some collect deaths like stamps. "I've died forty-seven times!

145
00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:54.680
Tokyo was my favorite.". What Fixing Health Fixed. Nobody predicted this (I predicted this): fixing health fixed everything

146
00:14:54.680 --> 00:15:00.380
else. Like pulling one thread and the whole sweater of human misery unravels.

147
00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:06.580
Climate Change: Solved the moment everyone realized they'd personally be alive to see the consequences.

148
00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:12.980
Amazing how much you care about sea levels when your beach house needs to last one hundred and fifty years.

149
00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:20.280
Poverty: Global G.D.P. tripled when you stopped losing productive years to preventable disease.

150
00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:24.160
It turns out the cure for poverty was curing everything else first.

151
00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:30.860
Education: When you live to one hundred and fifty, twenty years of education makes sense.

152
00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:38.160
Global literacy hit ninety-nine point nine percent. Innovation: Healthy brains think better.

153
00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:42.380
More breakthrough discoveries in twenty years than the previous two hundred.

154
00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:46.640
It's almost as if not poisoning your scientists improves their output.

155
00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:53.520
Peace: Hard to start a war when your citizens have one hundred and thirty years of remaining life expectancy.

156
00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:59.900
A one hundred and fifty-year-old is significantly less keen on dying for a flag than an eighteen-year-old.

157
00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:04.780
Recruitment posters don't work on people who've already been eighteen twice.

158
00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:10.680
Happiness: Not dying of preventable diseases makes people happier.

159
00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:18.440
I apologize for stating something so obvious. But given that you spent four thousand years not acting on it, apparently

160
00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:28.300
somebody needed to. Message from the Future. Dear Present You, This message comes from a world where your children live

161
00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:32.500
to one hundred and fifty. Where cancer is as treatable as a cold.

162
00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:38.700
Where depression has precise, effective treatments. Where aging is a choice, not a sentence.

163
00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:43.880
Where humanity collaborates instead of competing to see who can destroy things fastest.

164
00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:52.020
This world exists because you finally made one choice: You made healing people more profitable than killing them.

165
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:56.780
Your great-great-great grandchildren (who you'll meet) are grateful.

166
00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:01.860
P. S. The chocolate thing is real. For some genetics, it's medicine.

167
00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:08.020
Science is wonderful when you fund it. WISHONIA. What Comes After.

168
00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:15.480
You solved death, suffering, and scarcity. Now what? Some humans explore galaxies.

169
00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:21.400
Some become pure consciousness. Some perfect the sandwich. (The sandwich faction is the largest.

170
00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:28.480
This surprised no one.). Your network of decentralized institutes of health still exists, but it ran out of diseases.

171
00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:35.540
It pivots to making reality more interesting. Today's project: teaching gravity to be less clingy.

172
00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:40.860
Gravity is not cooperating. The universe notices you. It's impressed.

173
00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:44.720
You're invited to the Galactic Council. You bring potato salad.

174
00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:51.240
Everyone loves it. Potato salad saves the universe. You're still alive to see it.

175
00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:56.590
Because you followed the instructions in this book. Your Two Paths.

176
00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:01.900
You're at the fork. Path A: The Dystopia - You spent trillions on death.

177
00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:09.620
Got exactly what you paid for. Everyone died. Path B: Wishonia - You spent one percent on life.

178
00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:18.560
Nobody died. The choice is still yours. My planet chose Path B four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years ago.

179
00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:26.640
We're doing fine. In Path A, you spend one hundred percent on weapons and zero percent on cures.

180
00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:32.020
Everyone dies. In Path B, you redirect one percent to cures.

181
00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:40.780
Nobody dies. The math is simple. Even for humans. (Especially for humans, because you invented math and then refused to

182
00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:47.060
use it.) While you read this chapter, over two thousand people died of preventable diseases.

183
00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:53.980
(one hundred and fifty thousand per day equals one hundred and four per minute.) They did not get a vote on which path you

184
00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:58.180
chose. Make up your mind. There's no Door C. Choose wisely.

185
00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:06.820
Choose life. Choose the War on Disease. Your future self (who lives to one hundred and fifty) will thank you.

186
00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:15.200
*WISHONIA* *World Integrated System for High-Efficiency Optimization, Networked Intelligence, and Allocation* *Watched You

187
00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:18.630
Choose Wisely* *See You at the Party* *Bring Potato Salad*
